### V23-70 — the last three app suites, and a guard for the failure that hid them

V23-69 left three suites out because they did not collect: `blockchain-explorer` (1 error),
`miner` (3), `zk-circuits` (3). The errors were `No module named 'main'`,
`'production_miner'` and `'zk_cache'` — one shared cause. These three keep their modules at
the app root instead of under `src/`, so nothing on `pythonpath` reaches them and no import
of theirs has ever resolved.

The obvious fix reintroduces the bug V23-69 just finished removing. Putting an app root on
`sys.path` makes pytest derive `tests.test_...` for that app's test modules, because it walks
up from the test file past `__init__.py` directories to a basedir and shortens the name when
that basedir is importable. `tests` is already in `sys.modules` — it is the repo-root
package — so the app's tests either collide with it or silently shadow it.

So each of the three needs **both** halves: a `tests/conftest.py` that inserts its own app
directory, and deletion of that suite's `tests/__init__.py`. Either half alone is fine; only
the combination breaks, which is exactly the property that makes it easy to reintroduce. The
inserted entry is the app directory and never `apps/` — `apps/` sits above all sixteen test
directories and renames every one of them at once. None of the three suites use relative
imports, so dropping the package costs nothing. `apps/miner/src` also joins `pythonpath`,
since miner imports `miner_app.reinvestment` as well.

`tests/unit/test_suite_module_identity.py` now pins both rules: `apps/` is never on
`sys.path`, and no `tests` package has its own app root on `sys.path`. These are static
checks over the eighteen app test directories, so they fail on the introduction rather than
on the symptom — the V23-69 symptom was ten faucet tests reporting an unsigned transaction
against an endpoint that had signed correctly, which took a day to trace back to a `sys.path`
line in an unrelated app.

Independently confirmed clean: a collection-time probe over `sys.modules` reports every repo
file reachable under more than one module name. It finds three, all of them deliberate
aliases built by `tests/coordinator/test_ignored_modules.py:23`. No conftest or test module is
imported twice.

blockchain-explorer 11 passed and 4 xfailed, miner 58, zk-circuits 26. The four xfails are
pre-existing and honest: `TransactionSearch` and `BlockSearch` were removed in a refactor and
the endpoints take query parameters now.

**All sixteen app suites are collected.** Root 3378 → **3496**, blockchain-node 540, zero
failures.

