### V23-85 — the security gate that exited on a usage error, in a hook nothing installed · CONFIRMED → RESOLVED

Two independent failures, either of which alone would have been enough. The filed finding was
the second one.

#### It could not have passed

```yaml
- id: bandit
  args: [-c, pyproject.toml, -r, ., -x, cli/templates, tests/cli, tests/]
```

`-x` takes one comma-separated value. Written as three separate list items, `cli/templates`
goes to `-x` and `tests/cli` and `tests/` fall through to the positional slot argparse has
already filled with `.`:

```
$ pre-commit run bandit --hook-stage pre-push --all-files
bandit...................................................................Failed
- hook id: bandit
- exit code: 2

bandit: error: unrecognized arguments: tests/cli tests/
```

Exit 2 on a usage error, before opening a file. There is no input on which this hook passes.

#### Nothing installed it either

```
$ ls .git/hooks | grep -v sample
commit-msg  post-checkout  post-commit  post-merge  pre-commit  pre-push

$ cat .git/hooks/pre-push
#!/bin/sh
command -v git-lfs >/dev/null 2>&1 || { ... }
git lfs pre-push "$@"
```

That is git-lfs's hook, not pre-commit's — `.git/hooks/pre-commit` carries the
`# File generated by pre-commit` header and this one does not. `pre-commit install` with no
arguments installs the pre-commit hook and nothing else, and bandit was the only
`stages: [pre-push]` entry in the file. Every document in the repository that tells you how to
set this up says the bare command:

| document | line |
|---|---|
| `docs/development/5_developer-guide.md` | 38 |
| `docs/meta/installation-guide.md` | 67 |
| `docs/agents/AGENTS.md` | 238 |
| `skills/aitbc-software-setup/SKILL.md` | 281 |

Only the archived `docs/releases/v0.4.22/PRE_COMMIT_HOOKS_GUIDE.md` mentions
`--hook-type pre-push`, and nothing current points at it.

#### And there was no configuration to read

`-c pyproject.toml` has been in the args since the hook was added. There has never been a
`[tool.bandit]` section in that file — the only occurrence of the string is `bandit = "1.9.4"`
in the dev dependencies. The hook was also pinned at `rev: 1.8.3`, so if it had ever run it
would have run a different bandit from the one the project installs.

#### What it finds

Once invocable:

| scope | findings |
|---|---|
| everything on disk | 4,244 |
| tracked files only | 3,837 |
| tracked, excluding test files | 449 |
| tracked, excluding tests, MEDIUM severity and above | 36 |

The first two rows differ because bandit walks the filesystem and does not read `.gitignore`.
That run already passed `-x` for `venv/`; the 407 findings it still picked up outside version
control were 390 from `apps/coordinator-api/.venv/`, 16 from the vendored forge-std and
OpenZeppelin trees under `contracts/governance/lib/`, and 1 stray script. The `.venv/` share
includes 11 of the 21 HIGH findings, every one of them inside pip — its own `_internal` and
its vendored copies of requests and distlib.

Of the 3,837 tracked findings, 3,388 were `B101 assert_used` in test files. A gate that
reports four thousand things blocks nothing, so the hook now runs at
`--severity-level medium`, and `[tool.bandit]` in `pyproject.toml` holds the exclusions the
broken `-x` was reaching for.

`B104` (binding `0.0.0.0`) is skipped repo-wide with the reason written next to it: eight
sites, every one a service that runs in a container or behind the nginx proxy and binds the
one interface it has. B104 fires on the only spelling that works.

#### The 36

Down to **0**. Fixed rather than silenced, except where the finding was about a shape bandit
cannot see through:

**Real, fixed:**

- `scripts/utils/generate-api-keys.py` masks every key it prints — `print(f"API Key: {'*' * 32}")` —
  and then wrote all of them in cleartext to `/tmp/aitbc-api-keys.json` at the process umask.
  A fixed path any account on the host could read, and could have pre-created as a symlink.
  Now `tempfile.mkdtemp()` plus `os.open(..., O_EXCL, 0o600)`.
- `scripts/extract_openapi_specs.py` and `scripts/generate_openapi.py` set
  `WALLET_DIR=/tmp/test_wallet` — a keystore directory on a guessable shared path, with
  `KEYSTORE_PASSWORD=test-password` beside it. `generate_openapi.py` already had a
  `tempfile.mkdtemp()` two lines above and was not using it for this.
- Five `requests` calls with no timeout in `scripts/utils/cleanup_fake_gpus.py` and
  `scripts/utils/end_to_end_workflow.py`. requests waits forever by default.
- Two `urlopen` calls on URLs built from `$WALLET_RPC_URL` and `$GITEA_API_BASE`, both
  carrying credentials in an Authorization header, neither checking the scheme. `urlopen`
  honours `file:`. Both now reject anything that is not http or https — and both still carry
  `# nosec B310`, because B310 is a blacklist rule on the call and fires whatever guards
  precede it.
- Three staging files in the container deploy scripts written to fixed `/tmp` paths on the way
  to becoming root-owned unit files inside the container.

**False positive, marked:**

- `agent_stream.py:374` B608. The f-string interpolates `','.join('?' * len(spellings))` — a
  run of placeholders, never a value; every address arrives through the parameter tuple.
  sqlite3 has no way to bind a variable-length `IN` list, so this is the supported idiom.
  Lifted into a named `placeholders` variable so the marker sits on something readable.

**Deliberate, marked with the reason:**

- Ten `shell=True` calls across `scripts/deployment/deploy/container-deploy.py`,
  `deploy_container_with_miner.py` and `deploy_gpu_to_container.py`. The commands are literals
  composed with a container name that is the constant `"aitbc"` assigned inline; there is no
  input to inject, and they need a shell for `cd X && source Y && pip install` and
  `2>/dev/null || true`. Each marker carries the condition that invalidates it: a container
  name arriving from a flag or the environment.

#### Two things found on the way, filed separately rather than fixed here

- **22 tracked scripts hardcode `/home/oib/windsurf/aitbc`**, a path from a developer's old
  workstation that does not exist on this host. The three deploy scripts above are among them,
  which is why their `shell=True` calls were marked rather than restructured — they are dead
  code, and deciding that is a different change from making the hook work.
- **`scripts/testing/qa-cycle.py` has never done anything.** `run_cmd` passes command strings
  to `subprocess.run` with `shell=False`, so `"git fetch origin main"` is looked up as a single
  executable name; the resulting `FileNotFoundError` is swallowed by a bare `except`, and
  `main()` aborts at its first step.

#### Fix

`.pre-commit-config.yaml`:

```yaml
default_install_hook_types: [pre-commit, pre-push]
```

```yaml
  - repo: https://github.com/PyCQA/bandit
    rev: 1.9.4
    hooks:
      - id: bandit
        args: [-c, pyproject.toml, -r, ., --severity-level, medium]
```

`rev` moves 1.8.3 → 1.9.4 to match the project's own pin. `commit-msg` is deliberately absent
from `default_install_hook_types`: no hook declares that stage, and installing it would
displace the hand-written PILOT-79 ticket-tag guard for nothing.

`pyproject.toml` gains `[tool.bandit]` with `exclude_dirs` and the single `skips` entry.
Note that bandit matches `exclude_dirs` entries as plain substrings as well as globs, which is
why each is written with its surrounding slashes.

#### Verification

```
$ pre-commit run bandit --hook-stage pre-push --all-files
bandit...................................................................Passed
```

0 HIGH, 0 MEDIUM — down from 36 MEDIUM-and-above. 427 LOW remain below the gate.

`pre-commit run --all-files` passes every other hook, including `mypy-clean-apps`, `ruff`,
`ruff-format` and `openapi-specs-match-the-apps` — the last confirming that swapping
`scripts/extract_openapi_specs.py` onto a temporary `WALLET_DIR` still regenerates the specs
byte-identically. The one failure is `require-set-euo-pipefail-in-touched-scripts`, on 13
pre-existing `.sh` files this change does not touch; that hook is scoped to scripts in the
commit by design (V23-23), so `--all-files` is the wrong way to run it and its failure there
is expected.

Root suite: 6,284 passed, 272 skipped, exit 0 — the full 6,556, unchanged. The only app file
in this change is `agent_stream.py`, and the edit there is a comment plus a `# nosec` marker.

#### Operator step

This clone still has git-lfs's `pre-push` hook, and installing over it is an operator
decision, not one to take inside a shared working tree that deployed services run from:

```bash
pre-commit install
```

With `default_install_hook_types` set, that one command now installs both hook types. It is
safe to run over git-lfs's hook — pre-commit moves an existing hook to `pre-push.legacy` and
runs it before its own, so `git lfs pre-push` keeps happening. Confirmed in
`pre_commit/commands/hook_impl.py`, which calls `_run_legacy` before dispatching.

### V23-86 — a workstation path that outlived the workstation, in 24 tracked scripts · CONFIRMED → RESOLVED

`/home/oib/windsurf/aitbc` is a checkout on a developer's old machine. The repo is at
`/opt/aitbc`. 24 tracked `*.py`/`*.sh` files still name that path, and every one of them either
fails at its first command or operates on nothing.

Found while clearing the bandit findings for V23-85 — two of these scripts were among the ten
`shell=True` sites marked there. That PR left them in place deliberately: getting the hook to
run was one job, deciding what a dead script deserves is another.

#### Three of them were invisible

The obvious search misses a quarter of the problem:

```
$ grep -rln "/home/oib/windsurf" --include='*.py' --include='*.sh' . | grep -v '/venv/' | wc -l
21
$ git grep -l "/home/oib/windsurf" -- '*.py' '*.sh' | wc -l
24
```

`.gitignore:321` is `scripts/deployment/*`, with eight `!` exceptions below it. Everything else
under that directory — including the tracked `deploy/` subtree — is ignored, so `ripgrep`,
`ugrep --ignore-files` and every editor search that honours `.gitignore` skips files that are
in version control and get edited. `git grep` reads the index and sees them. The three hidden
ones were `deploy/deploy_container_with_miner.py`, `deploy/deploy_gpu_to_container.py` and
`deploy/deploy-explorer.sh`.

The 24th, `tests/verification/verify_windsurf_tests.py`, is not on `main` at all yet — it comes
back with the 90 files restored in V23-71 and is sitting in the unmerged stack.

#### What they point at

Almost nothing they name still exists:

| referenced | status |
| --- | --- |
| `gpu_miner_with_wait.py` | in no checkout, at no path, in no commit |
| `genesis_enhanced_devnet.yaml` | absent |
| `src/app/…` (coordinator-api) | package renamed to `coordinator_api` |
